        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="true" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="true">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <HouseholdOperatingConditions numberOfOccupants="3" coolingSeasonMonths="0" isClothesWasherEnergySaver="false" isLightingEnergySaver="true" areAppliancesEnergySaver="false">
                <Thermostat heatingDaytime="21" heatingNighttime="18" cooling="25" />
            </HouseholdOperatingConditions>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="0" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="1" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The majority of air leakage was observed around windows, particularly the master bedroom and kitchen/dining area. The kitchen range hood exhaust also had considerable air leakage. Additional air leakage at piping penetrations could be felt in the laundry area. The door in the buffered wall (Tyna's room) had air leakage along the edges. Suggested that air sealing activities be concentrated in these areas. </airSeal>
                <windows>Suggest replacement of all dual-pane windows with Energy Star rated triple-pane units. Suggest replacements units be selected from windows listed in the Greener Homes grant. 



Through the Canada Greener Homes Grant initiative, grants of either $125 or $250 per window rough opening are available when an ENERGY STAR certified or ENERGY STAR certified Most Efficient window is installed to replace an existing window. Replacing old, damaged or leaky windows with new ENERGY STAR certified products can help you save on energy, improve comfort and reduce noise. To determine eligibility of the product you are seeking to purchase, confirm that it is included on the list of eligible equipment as found on the Canada Greener Homes Grant webpage</windows>
                <WaterConservation>Suggest replacing shower heads and faucet aerators with low flow units.</WaterConservation>
            </RURComments>
            <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
                <Community>N/A</Community>
            </GreenerHomes>
        </Options>
